      "name": "Range Rover 4.4 Engine Repair Experts — FAQs",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#webpage"
      },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-1",
          "name": "Is the Range Rover SDV8 diesel engine reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can be dependable with proper maintenance, but EGR cooler failure and oil pump wear are well-documented issues as these engines age. Reliability depends heavily on service history and whether early symptoms, such as coolant loss or low oil pressure, were investigated promptly."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-2",
          "name": "What are the most common SDV8 faults?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The two most frequently reported issues are EGR cooler failure, which can allow coolant into the engine, and oil pump wear affecting oil pressure. Turbo wear is also worth checking on higher-mileage examples, particularly if you notice reduced power or unusual noise."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-3",
          "name": "Is the new BMW-sourced 4.4 petrol V8 reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The P530 is a newer engine and hasn't shown the same established fault pattern as the SDV8, but it's still a complex twin-turbo V8 worth maintaining carefully. We'd recommend the same attentiveness to warning lights and unusual noises regardless of the engine's age."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-4",
          "name": "Which Range Rover models use a 4.4 litre engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The SDV8 diesel has been fitted to the Range Rover L322 and L405 generations and Range Rover Sport, while the P530 petrol V8 appears in newer Range Rover and Range Rover Sport models. Confirming the exact engine code helps us give accurate advice."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-5",
          "name": "How much does a Range Rover 4.4 V8 engine replacement cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost depends on the engine variant, the extent of damage, and whether a repair, rebuild or full replacement is the right route. Given how costly these engines are, we assess each vehicle individually and provide a clear, itemised quote once diagnosis is complete."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-6",
          "name": "Should I repair or replace a failing SDV8 engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "This depends on what diagnosis finds. An EGR cooler or oil pump fault caught early can often be resolved through targeted repair, while extensive internal damage usually points toward a reconditioned or replacement engine. We'll explain the reasoning before recommending either option."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-7",
          "name": "Do reconditioned Range Rover 4.4 engines come with a warranty?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, reconditioned and replacement V8 engines are supplied with warranty cover. We'll confirm the specific terms for your engine and vehicle before any work is booked, which matters given the value involved."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-4.4#faq-question-8",
          "name": "What areas do you cover for Range Rover V8 engine work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We're based in Grays, Essex, and regularly support customers across Essex, London and the wider South East, alongside UK-wide enquiries for engine supply and fitting. Contact us to confirm availability for your location."
          }
        }
      ]
